  "year": 2025,
  "arxivId": "2407.16741",
  "abstract": "OpenHands is a community-driven platform for developing generalist AI agents that interact with the world through software. It provides a flexible and powerful framework for agents to execute code, interact with a command line, and browse the web, allowing them to perform complex tasks such as software engineering, web browsing, and data analysis.",
  "sections": [
    {
      "title": "The Core Idea",
      "content": "Imagine a platform where AI agents can interact with the world in a similar way to human developers. <strong>OpenHands</strong> is a community-driven platform that enables AI agents to write code, execute commands, and browse the web, making them generalist agents. This platform allows agents to perform complex tasks, such as software engineering, web browsing, and data analysis, by interacting with a <strong>bash shell</strong>, <strong>IPython server</strong>, and <strong>web browser</strong>.",
