    {
      "title": "How It Works",
      "content": "The OpenHands platform consists of three main components: <strong>agent abstraction</strong>, <strong>event stream</strong>, and <strong>runtime environment</strong>. The agent abstraction allows users to create and customize agents for various tasks. The event stream tracks the history of actions and observations, while the runtime environment executes actions and returns observations. This setup enables agents to interact with the world in a flexible and powerful way, allowing them to perform tasks such as <strong>code editing</strong>, <strong>web browsing</strong>, and <strong>data analysis</strong>.",
